## Clues

A1. Tops “Third Letter” with a postscript (4) ~ CAPS
A1 ^revealer: C + A + P.S.

A4. Knock back wigs in “Agony” (4) ~ SWIG
A4 ^revealer: SWIG (anag.)

A7. Fleet, twisted drama: “The Last of Sheila” (6) ~ ARMADA
A7 ^revealer: ARMAD + A ({/drama/} anag.)

A8. Restaged “Follies,” with final character in neighborhood bordering Hollywood (3,5) ~ LOSFELIZ
A8 ^revealer: LOS FELI + Z ({/Follies/} anag.)

A9. Cleaner snippet of “Merrily” solo (5) ~ LYSOL
A9 ^revealer: LYSOL (hidden)

A11. Twirling a mop, covering “Cool” (nineties style) in old-timey lighting (3,4) ~ OILLAMP
A11 ^revealer: O(IL L)AMP ({/a mop/} anag.)

A13. Soprano: “Nothing eclipses ‘Company’ . . . it’s a treat” (3-4) ~ SNOCONE
A13 ^revealer: S + NO-(CO)NE

A17. Crest cryptic grid (Sondheim’s sixth) (5) ~ RIDGE
A17 ^revealer: RIDG + E ({/grid/} anag.)

A19. Answer involves Tony and Maria—at first, they’re opposites (8) ~ ANTONYMS
A19 ^revealer: AN(TONY + M)S

A20. Note Seinfeld’s neighbor emulating the chronology of “Merrily We Roll Along” (6) ~ REMARK
A20 ^revealer: REMARK (rev.)

A21. Baker tries holding back journey into the woods, maybe (4) ~ TREK
A21 ^revealer: TREK (hidden rev.)

A22. Elaine Stritch has a home for “Someone in a Tree”? (4) ~ NEST
A22 ^revealer: NEST (hidden)

D1. Call “America” something rough, as a result of friction (6) ~ CALLUS
D1 ^revealer: CALL + U.S.

D2. Greeting Anita primarily in Spanish today (4) ~ AHOY
D2 ^revealer: A + {/HOY/}

D3. Pass it on: tango’s missing in Sondheim show (7) ~ PASSION
D3 ^revealer: PASSI(t)ON

D4. Aroma from suspicious meat entices lunching Londoners at first (5) ~ SMELL
D4 ^revealer: SMELL (first letters of {/suspicious meat entices lunching Londoners/})

D5. Saying, “I almost did regular excerpts from ‘Poems’ ” (5) ~ IDIOM
D5 ^revealer: I + DI(d) + OM (even letters of {/Poems/})

D6. In toga (Zero’s look) (4) ~ GAZE
D6 ^revealer: GAZE (hidden)

D10. Victor Kayden, misbehaving actor in “Dick Tracy” (3,4) ~ VANDYKE
D10 ^revealer: V + AN DYKE ({/Kayden/} anag.)

D12. Already arranged reinterpretation of Streep or Peters (6) ~ PRESET
D12 ^revealer: PRESET (anag.)

D14. After forty, person hunting gold slipper ultimately chasing nickel and neon (5) ~ NINER
D14 ^revealer: NI + NE + R

D15. Cargo tank oddly generating sound from “The Frogs”? (5) ~ CROAK
D15 ^revealer: CROAK (odd letters of {/cargo tank/})

